It is a standalone extraction of the "Token Bank / 鲸元券" feature and is
derived from the following upstream work:

  dsh-web — DeepSeek Harness (DSH) Web GUI 插件与主题全家桶
  https://github.com/zhu1090093659/dsh-web
  Copyright the dsh-web contributors
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

  Specifically the package `@linxin666/dsh-usage` (packages/dsh-usage), from
  which this project reuses:

  - assets/jingyuan-note.jpg — the whale-yuan note artwork
    (upstream source: packages/dsh-usage/assets/jingyuan-note.jpg, 1400x714).
    The file is redistributed unchanged.
  - the note layout stamped onto the artwork (denomination block, "whale yuan"
    caption, seal-red serial line) and its geometry ratios, as implemented in
    packages/dsh-usage/src/client/voucher.ts
  - the DeepSeek peak/off-peak price book and the Beijing peak-window clock
    (packages/dsh-usage/src/core/pricing.ts)
  - the per-day / per-provider / per-model ledger fold document shape and its
    defensive deserialization (packages/dsh-usage/src/core/ledger.ts)
  - the loopback trust fence semantics (socket address + Host header + browser
    same-origin markers) from dsh-web's shared host sources
  - the browser module-loader bundle convention
    (`window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id, factory })`) from dsh-web's built
    client bundle

Nothing from upstream is bundled beyond the artwork asset listed above; the
host and client halves in this package are an independent, smaller
implementation written for a standalone install (no dsh-web-settings family
bridge, no provider balance probes, no plan quotas, no sidebar foot card).

DeepSeek, DeepSeek Harness and the whale-girl character are properties of their
respective owners; this is an unofficial community plugin.
